Cooperative scheduling retains the original complete output
open import FrescoPrelude; open import Coop; run(test)
stdout : @M1 A1 M2 A2 M3 B1 M4 B2 M5 \nNothing : \[\|Just:\(\(\), Coop\.ResList \(\(\)\)\)\|Nothing\|\]$
args : --fresco --path=examples/handlers:examples:lib/stdlib

Cooperative handlers retain generic integer and boolean results
open import FrescoPrelude; open import Coop; (run(fun(){42}),run(fun(){true}))
stdout : (Just(42, Nil), Just(true, Nil)) : ([|Just:(Int, Coop.ResList (Int))|Nothing|], [|Just:(Bool, Coop.ResList (Bool))|Nothing|])
args : --fresco --path=examples/handlers:examples:lib/stdlib

Cooperative handlers retain contextual returned values
open import FrescoPrelude; open import Coop; effect Reader { Ask : () => Int; } handle ({var result=run(fun(){fun(){do Ask}}); switch(result) {case Just((f,_)) -> f() case Nothing -> 0}}) {case x -> x case <Ask => k> -> k(7)}
stdout : 7 : Int
args : --fresco --path=examples/handlers:examples:lib/stdlib

Queued cooperative resumptions retain order and caller effects
open import FrescoPrelude; open import Coop; effect Reader { Ask : (Int) => Int; } handle ({var result=run(fun(){if(fork()) {yield(); do Ask(1)} else {yield(); do Ask(2)}}); switch(result) {case Just((value,queue)) -> switch(queue) {case Cons(next,queue) -> switch(next(queue)) {case Just((other,_)) -> [value,other] case Nothing -> [value]} case Nil -> [value]} case Nothing -> []}}) {case xs -> xs case <Ask(n) => k> -> print(intToString(n)); k(n+40)}
stdout : 12[41, 42] : List Int
args : --fresco --path=examples/handlers:examples:lib/stdlib

Cooperative execution retains its Wild requirement
open import FrescoPrelude; open import Coop; sig pure : () -> Int fun pure() {var _=run(fun(){42}); 42} ()
exit : 1
stderr : @.*Type error: Type does not match the required type.*In expression: run\.
args : --fresco --path=examples/handlers:examples:lib/stdlib

Cooperative operations require their effect
